 Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Rep. Tom Barrett defends an even-leaning mid-Michigan swing seat against Democratic challenger William Lawrence, with a Green candidate also on the ballot. Professional raters are split: Cook, Fox News, Inside Elections, Sabato's Crystal Ball and the Economist call it a Tossup, while five other outlets rate it Lean Democratic for a flip. Betting markets put Lawrence's chances between 56 and 62 percent.\n\nThe only published polls, both sponsored by Democratic groups, show Lawrence ahead by about two points, but the newest dates to mid-August, so they carry limited weight. Barrett holds a large cash advantage, $2.9 million to Lawrence's $383,000, though outside groups have spent heavily against him while spending little on his behalf. October debates highlighted Trump's shadow and Barrett's town hall difficulties. The race tilts narrowly Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6654, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6515, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6531, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6941, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6328, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6566, "margin": 3.0}, {"d